// Fixture (not a standalone test): the imported half of bin/t_modparseerr.ax. Compiled on
// its own it is expected to be REJECTED -- the missing `:` below is deliberate. The point
// of the pair is that importing a module with parse errors must fail the IMPORTING build
// too (B5): ax_driver_load_module runs its own Parser, whose diags_count the driver used
// to ignore entirely, so this module's errors were printed and an executable was produced
// anyway (BUG#53's accept-then-miscompile class, applied to an imported unit).
pub fn ok(x: i64) -> i64:
    return x + 1

pub fn broken(x: i64) -> i64
    return x
